@* The MathML twin of SvgBox - same three arrival paths, because they are the same mechanism and a fix to
   one does not imply the other:

     [data-mi-static]  a fully static run   -> MARKUP frame, namespace decided by the parse context
     [data-mn-dynamic] a dynamic attribute  -> ELEMENT frame, created by the renderer
     [data-nested]     inside an <svg> that is inside the <math>

   ⚠️ MathML has no <foreignObject> equivalent here: Blazor's isMathMLElement() tests only the namespace,
   so nothing stops propagation. The real escape is <annotation-xml encoding="text/html">, which neither
   renderer implements. *@
<math data-math display="block">
    <mrow data-mrow>
        <mi data-mi-static>x</mi>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <mn data-mn-dynamic mathcolor="@Color">@Value</mn>
    </mrow>
    <svg data-svg-in-math viewBox="0 0 10 10" width="@Size" height="@Size">
        <circle data-nested cx="5" cy="5" r="4" />
    </svg>
</math>

@code {
    /// <summary>Bound to mathcolor so the mn is an element frame, not part of a static run.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string Color { get; set; } = "red";

    /// <summary>The number rendered in the dynamic mn.</summary>
    [Parameter] public int Value { get; set; } = 42;

    /// <summary>Bound to width/height so the nested svg is an element frame.</summary>
    [Parameter] public int Size { get; set; } = 10;
}
